  "query_preview": "/Through Saturday/...\nIssued at 1049 PM MDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nAn upper level high will be centered over the Great Basin on Sun and \nthen will weaken some on Mon.  Cross-sections show just enough mid \nlevel moisture with favorable lapse rates to allow for isold high \nbased showers mainly over Park county Sun aftn.  Otherwise it will \nbe dry with above normal temperatures.\n\nOn Mon, once again there is some mid level moisture embedded in weak \nNW flow aloft.  As a result, can't rule out isold high based showers \nover the high terrain.  Meanwhile, with rising 850-700 mb temps \nalong with downslope low level flow, highs will be near record highs \nacross portions of the plains as readings reach the mid 80's to \naround 90.\n\nOn Tue, a weak disturbance may affect the area with some increase in \nmid level moisture.  Thus may see a slightly better chc of high \nbased showers/isold tstms over the higher in the aftn.  Over nern \nCO, it will remain dry with highs remaining 10 to 15 degrees above \nnormal.\n\nBy Wed, the flow aloft will remain weak WNW. The ECMWF still shows \nsome lingering mid level moisture over the higher terrain while the \nGFS doesn't.  Overall, any high based shower activity should be \nrather isold.  Once again highs will be 10 to 15 degrees above \nnormal.\n\nFor Thu and Fri, the flow aloft will become more zonal by Fri with \nmainly dry conditions expected.  Highs both days will continue 10 to \n15 degrees above normal over much of the area.\n\nBy next Sat, the flow aloft will increase from the WSW as an upper \nlevel trough develops over the Pacific NW.  Meanwhile, there are \nsignificant disagreements between the ECMWF and GFS as to where this \nsystem will be by late Sun.  The ECMWF intensifies the upper level \ntrough and keeps it near the West Coast while the GFS moves it \nquickly into the nrn Rockies and Great Basin.  At this point, really \nhard to say which solution will pan out.  However, it looks warm and \ndry on Sat with highs from 10 to 15 degrees above normal.  For Sun, \nthere could be a chc of precip in the mtns late in the day based on \nthe faster GFS solution.  Meanwhile, will likely see another day of \nabove normal temperatures as well.",
